---
// Public security page (EN mirror of /ro/juridic/securitate/).
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
const lang = "en" as const;
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Data security"
  lang={lang}
  description="How we protect members' and exhibitors' data: encryption in transit, code-based access, audit trail, encrypted backups. Report a security issue."
>
  <div class="container" style="padding-block: 2.5rem 3.5rem;">
    <p class="sec-cale"><a href="/en/">Home</a> · Data security</p>
    <h1 class="sec-title">Data security</h1>
    <p class="sec-intro">
      We manage data that matters to our members: the studbook, show entries, the Judges' School records.
      Here is, briefly and honestly, what we do to keep it safe.
    </p>

    <h2>What we do</h2>
    <ul class="sec-lista">
      <li><strong>Encryption in transit.</strong> The whole site runs exclusively over HTTPS.</li>
      <li><strong>Code-based access with rate limiting.</strong> Internal areas (registry office, courses
        platform, administration) open only with individual codes; repeated failed attempts are blocked
        automatically, and codes can be revoked at any time.</li>
      <li><strong>Secrets live only on the server.</strong> The verification keys for codes and sessions never
        reach the public pages.</li>
      <li><strong>Audit trail.</strong> Sensitive registry operations (issuing, changes, deletions) are recorded
        with author and date.</li>
      <li><strong>Encrypted backups.</strong> Records have encrypted backup copies (AES-256), kept separately
        from the working systems; restoration is tested.</li>
      <li><strong>Data minimisation.</strong> We ask only for what the purpose requires, and public pages show
        only what must be public (e.g. owners' contact details do not appear in the web version of the
        catalogue). See also the <a href="/en/juridic/confidentialitate/">privacy policy</a> and
        <a href="/en/juridic/cereri-date/">personal data requests</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Up-to-date software.</strong> Components are updated regularly and the system is checked
        periodically for known vulnerabilities.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Where we use artificial intelligence</h2>
    <p class="sec-text">
      In two places, both with a human at the wheel:
    </p>
    <ul class="sec-lista">
      <li><strong>Reading pedigree certificates.</strong> When a litter is registered, the registry office may request
        automated reading of the two parents' certificates, to avoid transcribing thirty ancestry entries by hand. The
        result is a <strong>proposal</strong>, checked and saved by a person — nothing enters the studbook on its own.
        Details on which documents are sent and where are in the
        <a href="/en/juridic/confidentialitate/">privacy policy</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Judging exercises</strong> in the Judges' School, for wording the explanations in a candidate's
        feedback. The score itself is computed by a fixed formula, not by the model: the AI part accounts for at most
        6% of it, and the exercises do not affect the final examination or authorisation.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="sec-text">
      Everywhere else — entry validation, ring qualifications and titles, the catalogue, the studbook, the School's
      tests — the work is done by human-written, verifiable rules. No decision concerning a member, a dog or a
      candidate is taken automatically.
    </p>

    <h2>What we do not promise</h2>
    <p class="sec-text">
      No organisation can guarantee absolute security. What we do promise is that we take the measures above
      seriously, fix what is found as a priority, and, should an incident affect anyone's data, notify them as
      the law requires.
    </p>

    <h2>Found a security issue?</h2>
    <div class="sec-nota">
      Write to <a href="mailto:contact@cfc-royal.ro"><strong>contact@cfc-royal.ro</strong></a> with the subject
      "Security". Describe what you found and how to reproduce it; please do not access other people's data and
      do not disclose the issue publicly before we have had a chance to fix it. We reply as fast as we can, and
      we thank you — good-faith reports help everyone.
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .sec-cale { font-size: .85rem; color: var(--color-text-muted); margin: 0 0 .3rem; }
  .sec-cale a { color: var(--color-link); }
  .sec-title { color: var(--color-primary); }
  .sec-intro, .sec-text { color: var(--color-text-muted); max-width: 46rem; }
  h2 { color: var(--color-primary); margin-top: 1.6rem; font-size: 1.25rem; }
  .sec-lista { max-width: 46rem; display: grid; gap: .55rem; padding-left: 1.2rem; }
  .sec-lista li { line-height: 1.5; }
  .sec-lista a { color: var(--color-link); }
  .sec-nota {
    max-width: 46rem; margin-top: .6rem; padding: .85rem 1.1rem;
    background: #f7f1df; border: 1px solid var(--color-accent); border-left-width: 4px;
    border-radius: var(--radius); font-size: .95rem; color: var(--color-text);
  }
  .sec-nota a { color: var(--color-link); }
</style>
